# TPOWER Global Responsive Layout (Desktop-First)

Applies to **every page** on the website.

## Core principle

**Desktop is the master design.**

Mobile, tablet, and other breakpoints must **not** redesign the layout. Mobile is the desktop composition viewed through a smaller window — scale proportionally; do not restack, reorder, or simplify.

The experience must match premium brands where mobile is essentially a scaled desktop presentation, **not** a separate mobile website.

## Forbidden on mobile (unless a hard technical limitation)

Do **not**:

- Move components or change section order
- Stack content differently from desktop
- Replace 2-column layouts with stacked single-column layouts
- Replace grids with a different UI structure
- Turn card rows into vertical stacks (`grid-cols-4` → `grid-cols-1`, etc.)
- Remove cards, images, buttons, animations, or content
- Hide sections with `hidden md:block` / `md:hidden` for “simplification”
- Move CTAs or move images above/below text when desktop keeps them side-by-side
- Swap landscape images for portrait crops
- Change typography hierarchy (only scale sizes)

### Anti-patterns (avoid)

```tsx
// ❌ NOT allowed as the default responsive strategy
className="flex flex-col lg:flex-row"
className="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 xl:grid-cols-4"
className="hidden md:block"
// image stacked above text on mobile when desktop is Image | Text
```

## Required approach

Keep the **same visual composition** as desktop. Only scale:

- Font sizes
- Padding / gap / max-width
- Border radius (subtle)
- Overall density

Prefer:

- `overflow-x-auto` + horizontal swipe for card rows
- Fixed desktop column counts (`grid-cols-3`, `grid-cols-4`, `grid-cols-[0.9fr_1.1fr]`) at all breakpoints
- `min-w-[…]` on scroll rows so cards keep desktop proportions
- Proportional type: e.g. `text-sm md:text-base lg:text-lg` (same hierarchy)
- Aspect ratios that match desktop (do not restyle to portrait)

### Preferred patterns

```tsx
// ✅ Image | Text at every width — only scale gap/padding/type
className="grid grid-cols-[0.9fr_1.1fr] items-center gap-3 p-3 sm:gap-6 sm:p-5 lg:gap-10 lg:p-6"

// ✅ 3 (or 4) cards stay in one row; swipe if needed
<div className="overflow-x-auto pb-2">
  <div className="grid min-w-[720px] grid-cols-3 gap-3 md:min-w-0 md:gap-6">
    {/* cards */}
  </div>
</div>
```

## Examples

| Desktop | Mobile (correct) | Mobile (wrong) |
|---------|------------------|----------------|
| Image \| Text | Image \| Text (smaller) | Image above Text |
| 4 cards in a row | Same 4-card row + horizontal scroll | 1-column stack |
| Silver \| Gold \| Platinum | Same 3-card row + swipe | Stacked cards |
| CTA copy \| artwork | Same two columns scaled | Artwork moved above copy |

## Carousel / slider

Horizontal scrolling is preferred over layout changes. Cards keep desktop proportions — do not resize cards independently per breakpoint.

## Typography & images

- Scale fonts proportionally; keep hierarchy
- Keep spacing ratios
- Keep desktop image aspect ratios
- Never crop critical subjects; never replace landscape with portrait for “mobile fit”

## Interaction with other rules

- Overrides the old “mobile first / cards stack” guidance in the visual system
- Works with Games/VIP visual quality and page-depth standards — quality stays high; **composition stays desktop**
- Chinese/English SEO and brand rules are unchanged

## Completion gate

A page is not responsively complete if mobile looks like a different product. Desktop and mobile should look almost identical — **size changes, layout does not**.
